# §3.3: a public agent artifact fetched by a browser from another origin MUST be
# permitted through standard cross-origin controls. These three lines are the
# whole of this site's reason to exist, so the deploy target has to honour this
# file (or the equivalent vercel.json beside it). GitHub Pages cannot set a
# response header at all and is disqualified for that reason.
/agents/agent-manifest.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60
/agents/marrow_point.network.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
